(
    title: "# Release evidence",
    produced_by: [
        "Produced by `cargo xtask ci --profile release`. No registry action was",
        "performed: no publish, no tag, no release, no credential use.",
    ],
    source_heading: "## Source",
    worktree_clean: "- Worktree: clean, including untracked files",
    candidate_version_suffix: "(both product crates, inherited from `[workspace.package]`; `ph-veml7700-als-conformance` pins the `0.0.0` sentinel and is never published)",
    deny_pass_suffix: "advisory, source, and licence policy pass",
    archive_heading: "## Prepublication archive",
    archive_intro: [
        "This is the archive Cargo builds from the tree above. It is **not** the",
        "byte-identical artifact a later `cargo publish` uploads: publishing",
        "repackages from the source tree. Publish only from this same unchanged",
        "clean pinned tree, then download the registry archive and verify its",
        "checksum and contents against this record.",
    ],
    inventory_heading: "### File inventory and per-entry digests",
    inventory_intro: [
        "Read from the `.crate` archive, not from the unpacked directory: the",
        "unpacked copy accumulates `target/` output once its tests run.",
        "",
        "SHA-256 of each entry's contents. Comparing two records entry by entry",
        "is what distinguishes a commit restamp from edited content, because",
        "the archive checksum changes in both cases and the file names change",
        "in neither. Only `.cargo_vcs_info.json` may differ between records",
        "for the same reviewed tree.",
    ],
    manifest_heading: "### Normalized manifest",
    vcs_heading: "### VCS metadata",
    missing_vcs: "{ \"error\": \"no .cargo_vcs_info.json in the archive\" }",
    test_boundary_heading: "## Test boundary",
    test_boundary: [
        "Two different things were tested, and the distinction matters:",
        "",
        "- **Standalone package tests** ran against the unpacked archive above.",
        "  They establish that the published crate builds and passes its own tests",
        "  in isolation.",
        "- **Driver-versus-model conformance** ran only in the repository.",
        "  `tests/device_model.rs` and the path-only `ph-veml7700-als-model`",
        "  dev-dependency are excluded from the package on purpose, so the archive",
        "  cannot rerun them. Model conformance is repository-level evidence and",
        "  must never be cited as package-level evidence.",
        "",
        "`ph-veml7700-als-model` is repository-only and unpublished.",
    ],
    not_established_heading: "## Not established",
    not_established: [
        "This evidence covers artifact identity and the implemented host boundary.",
        "It establishes no physical-device, electrical, optical, or calibrated",
        "behavior, and it is not a decision to publish.",
    ],
